# T0168 — Mesh suggested links

**Task:** T0168 (id `181`) — Mesh: suggested links (tags/titles first, embeddings later)
**Parent:** T0159 (id `172`) — Mesh: relationship graph, backlinks and focus view (epic)
**Depends on:** T0160, T0162, T0178, T0179, T0181, T0183, T0184, T0208 — all complete
**Required by:** T0300 golden sets (blocked) — record accept/dismiss only; do not build the corpus
**State at plan:** `ready` · Priority: low · Project: TaskMesh (4)
**Branch (after approval):** `T0168-suggested-links`

Propose links the user accepts or rejects. Never create a link until Accept. Embeddings already live in the knowledge index (T0208); this task does not add pgvector or a new model host.

## Decisions

1. **Own table, not `entity_links`.** `entity_links.origin` is only `manual` | `mention`, and a suggestion is not a graph edge. New `ai_link_suggestions`: per user, directed source and target (entity type + id), score `0..1`, one-line reason, status `pending` | `accepted` | `dismissed` | `rejected`, optional `audit_id`. Unique on user + both ends. A dismissed or rejected pair is never suggested again for that user, in either direction. An accepted pair is not suggested again either. Existing `entity_links` between the two records (any relation or origin) suppress the pair.
2. **Candidates, deterministic, visibility-scoped.** For the open record, SQL over records that user can see:
   - shared tags
   - the other record’s title or description contains this record’s display number or a distinctive title token, and there is no `#` mention link already
   - same ToDo list item parent, or same board
   - best cosine similarity from `knowledge_chunks` via the existing `semanticEntityScores` helper
   Cap the pending list (about 8). Subject types are the ones that already mount the links panel: task, todo, idea, document. The other end may be any linkable entity type.
3. **Score.** Register feature `links` (small, no tools). When the user’s route can run, send a small batch of minimized pairs (display number, title, short excerpt, tag names) through the policy, redaction, and audit path. The model returns a match percent and one one-line reason. A model “no” is stored `rejected`. When the route cannot run (no key, feature off, budget, project AI ceiling), still show heuristic hits with a fixed reason (`shared tags`, `mentioned by title`, `same list`, `same board`, `similar text`) and a deterministic score. Embedding and model calls skip a pair when either project is excluded from AI. Heuristics that stay in SQL still run.
4. **Accept and dismiss.** Accept inserts a manual `references` link from the suggestion source to its target (same direction the Mesh prototype already posts) and sets `accepted`. Dismiss sets `dismissed`. Both write `ai_output_feedback` when the row has an audit id. Suggestions themselves never write `entity_links`.
5. **UI.** A Suggestions block on `EntityLinksPanel`: display number, title, match percent, reason, Accept, Dismiss. Empty block stays quiet (no heading clutter when there is nothing pending). The same rows feed `MeshPanel`, which already draws the dashed suggestion card. Mesh Accept and Dismiss call this API so a dismiss survives reload; today Mesh only hides a card locally and posts a link with no dismissal row.
6. **When it runs.** On demand when the links panel or the Mesh tab loads that record, not a whole-instance sweep. Refresh is the same request. No new job type.
7. **Schema.** One Drizzle migration. Update `docs/database/` and run `npm run docs:sync-schema`. Finish-up is a MINOR bump. `FEATURES.md` gets one line. `RELEASE_NOTES.md` gets a New Functionality bullet.

## Scope

1. Migration, service, and routes: list for one record, accept, dismiss.
2. Prompt `links` v1, feature route entry, audit feature id `links`.
3. Panel section and Mesh wiring.
4. Tests for candidate filtering (already linked, dismissed, invisible) and for accept creating exactly one manual `references` row.
5. `npm run lint` clean.

## Out

- A second embeddings stack or Ollama install (T0208).
- Golden-set sentences (T0300).
- Auto-accept, or any write to `entity_links` except the user’s Accept.
- New record drawers. Suggestions for project, board, canvas, wiki, image board, and to-do list appear only when that record is the other end of a suggestion on a task, todo, idea, or document, or as a Mesh ghost.

## Acceptance

- Opening a Task, ToDo, Idea, or Document can show suggested records with a match percent and a reason. Nothing is linked until Accept.
- Accept adds one manual References link and the suggestion leaves the list. Dismiss removes it and it does not return on reload.
- A pair that is already linked is not suggested.
- With AI unavailable, heuristic suggestions still appear. With AI available, the stored reason can be the model’s one-line reason and the call is audited.
- The Mesh suggestion card for the focused record uses the same rows, and Dismiss there also sticks.
- `npm run lint` is clean.

## Confirm before implementation

1. Heuristic suggestions still show when the model route cannot run.
2. Dismiss (and reject) is permanent for that user and that pair, even if the text later changes.
3. Mesh cards are wired in this task, not left for a follow-up.
